@startuml Asset Movement Request, Approval, and Completion
title Asset Movement Request, Approval, and Completion

actor "Monitor Staff" as MonitorStaff
participant "Monitor App" as MonitorApp
participant "Backend" as Backend
database "PostgreSQL Database" as DB
participant "WebSocket Manager" as WS
actor "Registration Staff" as RegStaff
participant "Registration App" as RegApp
participant "Checkpoint Node\n(ESP32 Firmware)" as Node
participant "MQTT Broker" as MQTT

MonitorStaff -> MonitorApp: Select asset and request movement
MonitorApp -> Backend: POST /assets/movement/request
Backend -> DB: Create movement request\nstatus = pending
Backend -> DB: Update asset flow_status\nmovement_requested
DB --> Backend: Commit success
Backend -> WS: Broadcast asset_movement_requested
WS -> MonitorApp: Update asset status
WS -> RegApp: Show pending movement request

RegStaff -> RegApp: Approve movement request
RegApp -> Backend: POST /assets/movement/approve
Backend -> DB: Validate registration node
Backend -> DB: Update movement request\nstatus = approved
Backend -> DB: Update asset flow_status\nin_transit
DB --> Backend: Commit success
Backend -> WS: Broadcast asset_movement_approved
WS -> MonitorApp: Show approved / in transit
WS -> RegApp: Remove or update pending request

Node -> MQTT: Publish RFID detection at destination
MQTT -> Backend: Deliver detection message
Backend -> DB: Load asset and active movement request

alt Asset detected at approved destination
    Backend -> DB: Complete movement request
    Backend -> DB: Update assigned room and current room
    Backend -> DB: Set asset flow_status = available
    DB --> Backend: Commit success
    Backend -> WS: Broadcast asset_updated
    Backend -> WS: Broadcast asset_movement_completed
    WS -> MonitorApp: Update asset row and movement status
    WS -> RegApp: Update asset table
else Asset detected at wrong destination
    Backend -> DB: Keep asset in transit or mark wrong_location
    Backend -> WS: Broadcast asset_updated
    WS -> MonitorApp: Show warning
    WS -> RegApp: Show warning
end

@enduml